IMPORT prelude

-- Presbyterian Church Ordinance 1876 (Singapore) -- who may sell the old chapel land held under Indenture No. 215 (s 2), what the
-- sale may cover and what the sellers may do to complete it (s 2), where the net proceeds go and what they may be spent on (s 3(1)),
-- on what trusts the new building is held (s 3(2)), and when a purchaser is safe (s 3(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PCO1876.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries
-- no amendment annotation. The Ordinance is dated 24 March 1876.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0243 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance is three sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person
-- outside the congregation it matters in one place: buying the land comprised in Indenture No. 215 from the trustees, and whether the
-- purchaser's receipt is a good discharge (s 3(3)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the identity of the land beyond its description as the land "comprised in and demised by" Indenture
-- No. 215 of 25 January 1827 (whether a parcel is that land is a stated fact); the content of the trusts in the grant of 6 May 1875,
-- beyond the purpose the preamble recites; what counts as "costs and expenses attending the sale"; what happens if the costs exceed
-- the price (the text does not say); whether the sale ever took place (the deposit does not say).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Presbyterian Church Ordinance 1876 -- the sale of the old chapel land`

§§ `2 -- who may sell`

-- s 2: "The said trustees, William Jeffrey, John James Greenshields, Matthew Little, Robert Jamie, John Anderson, Robert Little, M.D.,
-- and John Stowe Young, or the survivors of them, or any 2 or more of such surviving trustees who are for the time being resident
-- within the Colony may sell and dispose of the said piece or parcel of land ..."
--
-- Three alternatives are encoded: (a) the seven named trustees together; (b) "the survivors of them", that is every surviving named
-- trustee acting together, wherever resident; (c) any 2 or more surviving named trustees, all of whom are resident in the Colony.
-- Only the seven named persons can ever be in a selling group: a trustee appointed later is not named in s 2. Reading "the
-- survivors" to include a single sole survivor is an inference (the text uses the plural); it is encoded that way. Limb (a) is a
-- special case of (b) while all seven live, so the encoding tests (b) and (c) only.
DECLARE SellingGroup HAS
    `every member is one of the seven named trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every member is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes every surviving named trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of members` IS A NUMBER
    `every member is resident in the Colony` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the group` IS A SellingGroup
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consists of surviving named trustees` IF
        `the group`'s `every member is one of the seven named trustees`
    AND `the group`'s `every member is alive`
    AND `the group`'s `number of members` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `the group` IS A SellingGroup
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may exercise the power of sale` IF
        `consists of surviving named trustees` `the group`
    AND (    `the group`'s `includes every surviving named trustee`
         OR (    `the group`'s `number of members` AT LEAST 2
             AND `the group`'s `every member is resident in the Colony`))

§§ `2 -- what may be sold, and what the sellers may do`

-- s 2 (continued): "... the said piece or parcel of land comprised in and demised by the hereinbefore recited indenture of lease,
-- No. 215, made between the said United Company of Merchants of England trading to the East Indies, of the one part, and the said
-- C. H. Thompson, of the other part, dated 25 January 1827, and also all erections and buildings which have been erected and are now
-- standing on the said premises, with power also to execute assurances, give effectual receipts for the purchase money, and do all
-- other acts and things for completing such sale as they, or the survivors of them, or any 2 or more of such survivors, think proper."
--
-- The power is confined to the Indenture No. 215 land and the buildings on it. The buildings are those "now standing" (in 1876): a
-- building put up after the Ordinance is not named (a reading of "now"). The preamble recites that the trustees' power to sell under
-- the 1866 indenture was in doubt; the Ordinance confers a power of sale, not a power to borrow, so mortgaging is encoded as not
-- conferred (an inference from the words "sell and dispose of ... for completing such sale").
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `sell the Indenture 215 land`
    `sell buildings standing on it in 1876`
    `sell a building put up on it after the Ordinance`
    `execute assurances for the sale`
    `give effectual receipts for the purchase money`
    `do other acts for completing the sale`
    `sell other land of the congregation`
    `mortgage the Indenture 215 land`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the section 2 power` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `sell the Indenture 215 land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell buildings standing on it in 1876` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `execute assurances for the sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `give effectual receipts for the purchase money` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `do other acts for completing the sale` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the group` IS A SellingGroup, `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group may do the act` IF
        `may exercise the power of sale` `the group`
    AND `is within the section 2 power` `the act`

§§ `3(1) -- the net proceeds, who receives them, what they may be spent on`

-- s 3(1): "The moneys to arise from such sale, after deducting the costs and expenses attending the sale or otherwise incurred in
-- relation thereto, shall be paid to the trustees, or continuing acting trustees for the time being, of the said piece or parcel of
-- land so granted by Her Majesty the Queen as hereinbefore mentioned for the purpose of erecting and building on such land or any part
-- thereof a new church or chapel or other place of worship ... and shall be applied by such trustees to the building of such church
-- or chapel only."
--
-- The purpose clause names "a new church or chapel or other place of worship" on the granted land; the application clause then
-- confines the money to "the building of such church or chapel only". Both are encoded: the money may be spent only on building a
-- church or chapel on the granted land. Whether a building that is an "other place of worship" but not a church or chapel qualifies is
-- encoded as no, on the word "only" (a reading; the two clauses could be read together the other way).
GIVEN `the gross price` IS A NUMBER, `the costs of sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the net proceeds` IS `the gross price` - `the costs of sale`

DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF
    `the trustees of the land granted by the Crown`
    `the selling trustees`
    `the London Missionary Society`
    `the members of the congregation`

GIVEN `the payee` IS A Payee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the payee section 3 names` IF
    CONSIDER `the payee`
    WHEN `the trustees of the land granted by the Crown` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Outlay IS ONE OF
    `building a new church on the granted land`
    `building a new chapel on part of the granted land`
    `building another kind of place of worship on the granted land`
    `building a church on other land`
    `repairing the old chapel`
    `the general expenses of the congregation`
    `buying more land`

GIVEN `the outlay` IS AN Outlay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeds may be applied to` IF
    CONSIDER `the outlay`
    WHEN `building a new church on the granted land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `building a new chapel on part of the granted land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3(2) -- the trusts of the new building`

-- s 3(2): "The building when erected shall be held subject to the trusts set out in the grant above recited, and dated 6 May 1875."
-- The preamble recites that the grant was made "in trust, for the purpose of having a building or buildings erected thereon for
-- religious worship and use of the members of any denomination of Christians holding as their confession of faith the ecclesiastical
-- documents received by the different branches of the Presbyterian Church, and known as the Westminster Standard".
--
-- The trusts themselves are in the 1875 grant, which was not retrieved. The encoding uses only the purpose recited in the preamble: a
-- recital, not an enacting provision, and nothing in it says the grant contains no other terms.
GIVEN `holds the Westminster Standard as its confession of faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a denomination of Christians` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the recited purpose of the 1875 grant` IF
    `is a denomination of Christians` AND `holds the Westminster Standard as its confession of faith`

§§ `3(3) -- the purchaser`

-- s 3(3): "The receipts for the purchase money given by the persons exercising the power of sale hereby conferred shall be sufficient
-- discharges to the purchasers, who shall not be bound to see to the application of such purchase money."
--
-- The receipt must come from persons exercising the s 2 power, so a receipt from a group that cannot exercise it is not made a
-- discharge by s 3(3). Once a good receipt is given, what the trustees later do with the money does not touch the purchaser.
GIVEN `the group` IS A SellingGroup, `the group gave a receipt for the purchase money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receipt is a sufficient discharge to the purchaser` IF
        `may exercise the power of sale` `the group`
    AND `the group gave a receipt for the purchase money`

GIVEN `the proceeds were misapplied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is bound to see to the application of the money` IF FALSE
